# Agent Instructions

Please refer to the following files for agent rules and workflows:
- `.github/copilot-instructions.md`
- `.github/AGENTS.md`

Always refer to and follow the processes defined in the .agent/skills/ directory before proposing code changes.
All AI coding assistants and agents should follow the workflow skills defined in `.agent/skills/` (and `.github/skills/` if applicable) and strictly adhere to the guidelines provided in these documents.

## Available Slash Commands

When a user invokes a slash command, follow the corresponding workflow in `.github/skills/`:

- `/ideate` -> `idea-refine`
- `/spec` -> `spec-driven-development`
- `/plan` -> `planning-and-task-breakdown`
- `/implement` -> `incremental-implementation`
- `/tdd` -> `test-driven-development`
- `/debug` -> `debugging-and-error-recovery`
- `/review` -> `code-review-and-quality`
- `/launch` -> `shipping-and-launch`
- `/ci-cd` -> `ci-cd-and-automation`

